WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.180
SBOMs can become misleading when quality is not maintained.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:18.040
Common issues include missing components, duplicate components, unknown versions, ambiguous names, missing license data, stale dependency records, incorrect relationships, missing build metadata, and tool limitations.

3
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:25.260
A long SBOM is not automatically a useful SBOM if consumers cannot trust the identity and scope of its components.

4
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.280
Quality should be measured by usefulness, not by file size.

5
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.200
Validation should be part of the release workflow.

6
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:45.100
Teams can check required metadata, compare generated SBOMs across builds, verify hashes where practical, confirm that release artifacts match the declared scope, and review major dependency changes.

7
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:53.200
If a component appears, disappears, changes version, or changes relationship unexpectedly, the change should be explained before the release is approved.

8
00:00:53.480 --> 00:01:01.480
Drift happens when the SBOM no longer matches the source, build, dependency set, platform packaging, or release artifact.

9
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:14.220
It can occur because optional features changed, a package manager resolved a different version, generated code was updated, a platform SDK changed, or installer contents were modified after SBOM generation.

10
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:20.320
Drift is especially likely when SBOMs are generated once and then treated as static paperwork.

11
00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:27.380
Release gates should make drift visible before publication so teams can fix the record or regenerate it.

12
00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.940
Treat SBOM quality as continuous maintenance.

13
00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:39.840
Define required fields, review exceptions, fix tool configuration, document manual additions, and assign owners for quality decisions.

14
00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.260
The goal is not perfection on day one.

15
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:49.960
The goal is a trustworthy, repeatable inventory that improves over time and remains connected to the product's real build and release process.

16
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.380
Quality review should become routine, not a special audit scramble at the end.

17
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.040
Release records can show these trends.
